  HseTopic(number: 14, title: 'Human Factors, Human Reliability & Safety-Critical Task Management', content: 'TOPIC 14 – Human Factors, Human Reliability & Safety-Critical Task Management\n\nPurpose\nProvide systematic controls for human factors, human reliability & safety-critical task management in UAE workplaces and projects.\n\nTechnical requirements and field application\n1. Use approved company standards, risk assessments and task-specific procedures; verify current jurisdiction and client requirements.\n2. Define performance criteria, competent roles, inspection evidence, escalation triggers and emergency arrangements.\n3. Define scope, roles, applicable requirements and acceptance criteria before work begins.\n4. Identify routine, non-routine, abnormal and emergency conditions; include workers, contractors and affected interfaces.\n5. Apply elimination and substitution first, then engineering controls, administrative controls and PPE as the final layer.\n6. Use competent personnel, approved procedures, suitable equipment and documented authorization where required.\n7. Inspect controls before use and at risk-based intervals; remove defective equipment from service and record disposition.\n8. Stop work and reassess when scope, conditions, personnel, equipment, weather or interfaces change.\n9. Record evidence, communicate deficiencies, assign accountable owners and verify effectiveness before closure.\n\nField records and verification\n- Maintain a controlled register identifying the activity/equipment, location, responsible owner, inspection or review date, status, deficiencies and closeout evidence.\n- Verify controls in the field rather than relying only on signatures or document completion.\n- Record deviations, immediate safeguards, corrective action owner, due date and effectiveness check.\n\nUAE application\nApply the current requirements of the relevant UAE authority, emirate, client and operator. Confirm the approved site procedure and competent-pers